[{"id":"VRCE-3-19-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":1,"english":"Then the grim Śūrpanakhā, coming to Rāghava's asylum pointed out to the Rākşasas those brother in company with Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f8a8ebd9723835e9e9baaacfd29579f5d273efd6814c24f714a5157d7a88aef","compact":"b07bb7fe129683b1b8a7dd4c75e32dde391314435aa28bc3ed075814031d28dc","nasal":"b07bb7fe129683b1b8a7dd4c75e32dde391314435aa28bc3ed075814031d28dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":2,"english":"And they saw the mighty Rāma seated in the cottage in company with Sītā, and ministered to by Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.733,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b1e4ce2d9991582fe0b0e5fb0f994dd293e2cc040cef14890b2158f65d45c68a","compact":"d72a0006be5a0fd4f9a34f72c7365da3f17fcf5f0f419f835dc7fa18f21def9c","nasal":"d72a0006be5a0fd4f9a34f72c7365da3f17fcf5f0f419f835dc7fa18f21def9c"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":3,"english":"And seeing her, as well as the Rākşasas who had come, Rāma remarked to his brother, Lakşınaņa of flaming energy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9126a6e3a50e39cb06a86e048172d31026d160bf04d9c31d3e5bf43cb2ddb201","compact":"dfedb20f33c996d6e5d808c006e81c620ee2433c75adf3a3d896128ec099de6a","nasal":"2639a34247657cacf882c594b3ec98c4a85a78cb1d646a32bad2cbb035cf28eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":4,"english":"O Sumitrā's son, do you for a while guard Sītā. I shall slay these that have come to this asylum here.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4279b6e5886e657f497d7e609d423e196d2aae18962db11727d4519b344c607b","compact":"e56f6495bfadf90cb6a8b513566fcee9f601e40c9ce7af249b1f76b7cbd2af52","nasal":"9c090c32d3eb785695cde9389a010a74c5f7a764ffac3d430c0fb6d10dac6a55"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":5,"english":"Hearing these words of Rāma versed in the knowledge of self, Lakşmaņa honoured his speech by saying, So be it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.765,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b8e04f3e144adfceee0939a9d9a39562dfcd9f58b89405b852c78d37c6873ae","compact":"1019f5eddd5e307521181df1dc3af5b3ea567c368ad80c9cc9db69cdb88d5f7e","nasal":"1019f5eddd5e307521181df1dc3af5b3ea567c368ad80c9cc9db69cdb88d5f7e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":6,"english":"And the righteous Rāghava strung his mighty bow decked with gold; and addressed the Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c32f876aa1756bbb9882021ffa37b207dbb524f67515487c9176606be2967cd6","compact":"d7054796be45465a90ecc53d6498bcac62a0a7f3eb2420ac5b2c00a5c02eaef1","nasal":"d7054796be45465a90ecc53d6498bcac62a0a7f3eb2420ac5b2c00a5c02eaef1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":7,"english":"We that have entered into this untraceable forest of Dandaka in company with Sītā are the sons of Dasaratha, the brothers, Rama and Lakşmana. Why do you intend to do injury to us. Subsisting on fruits and roots, having our senses under control, carrying on asceticism and leading a Brahmacarya life, we are passing our days in the forest of Dandaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"18f672962658119afd9391ee1878fd3fad1fa577485d085be0308e0f2a565a86","compact":"b151ef40f0f583bb9ff7e65f365d4e6694254953fc1cb4378b8b57a2b917309f","nasal":"bcfa298f9ce87d4678b1c02b470c01affb7fb91c9a8c37606055e69d88e00ee4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":8,"english":"We that have entered into this untraceable forest of Dandaka in company with Sītā are the sons of Dasaratha, the brothers, Rama and Lakşmana. Why do you intend to do injury to us. Subsisting on fruits and roots, having our senses under control, carrying on asceticism and leading a Brahmacarya life, we are passing our days in the forest of Dandaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3daa262b156dd680f7f69ce7f1be04148d96e5b8605b3b62c68974a74b98d585","compact":"c40c3053c316dd54d0abfa72c3c14a8673d8e6f33580d90550f2b51fe403a93a","nasal":"9605340192fe3614824c9eb1c6cdf9fa828cc49570824c47215c8f08d3dc2971"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":9,"english":"It is do destroy you, wicked, and troublesome that I equipped with the bow have come here at the desire of the saints.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.612,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d74bc5eaa85b3c4aedff1b9a53d0aa2f53be25da5abb83a19f4eb1fa3bf1d10b","compact":"af0c82cdccb9c1ca4ffcd8612110bd28d8db8e60b47427c7f57eb2aa5d5be9e9","nasal":"c7b7bbffd4f50f7eafdee2b552e4ac970cacc796f2ea91a49ea69de918c2f322"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":10,"english":"Stay there content you should not move further. If you have a care for your lives, desist, you rangers of the night.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.646,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9f69c930f6c3aaf8e1a311fa455d45e3aaffbd86462c4fce69869cb76b7c5f8","compact":"b6a5863d091c24c012fec0010bdf599db18b9ca2a824aaf0405efc8e5e4d5ee9","nasal":"b6a5863d091c24c012fec0010bdf599db18b9ca2a824aaf0405efc8e5e4d5ee9"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":11,"english":"Hearing those words of his, those fourteen grim Rākşasas bearing darts in their hands, exceedingly enraged, with their eyes reddened, breathing high spirits, harshly said to the sweetspeeched Rāma, having his eyes reddened whose prowess they had not seen before.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0843eab0cf83dabfa013947a6a457f8d9636ccbdf3a08bfbd13d43d0f8d1cbc1","compact":"1c57c85fb28102d7441df4724f286caa806c7dfbc