nskritLocator":"3019014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b379c18ad68097cfc8592f1e1015948300fbdfb0b0f7aba9f0976a84413833a9","compact":"b5d0d7cad68f005b2725ed69fa8bdb1562218ecaa9c0a3898b642a03bfc1b12f","nasal":"b5d0d7cad68f005b2725ed69fa8bdb1562218ecaa9c0a3898b642a03bfc1b12f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":15,"english":"In consequence of the parighas (iron-clubs), darts, and pattisas (a kind of sharp-edged sword) discharged by our arms, you will surely lose your life, along with your prowess, and this bow which you press with your hand.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.849,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d4527b51bbd85ff2aa8aafb47fd5e21bc32b11668314094e4456ce41dd0d12f","compact":"4093843feb5fcac562cf11047c2693633ff3085e1dfc796b1166295dcadc1852","nasal":"4093843feb5fcac562cf11047c2693633ff3085e1dfc796b1166295dcadc1852"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":16,"english":"Having said this in wrath, those fourteen Rākşasas, uplifting their weapons and daggers rushed towards Rāma. And discharged darts at the invincible Rāghava. Thereupon Kākutstha by means of shafts decked with gold, cut off those fourteen darts of theirs.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.648,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-14","DUTT-3-20-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6f7ce490a70f198364513cda53986d13448de33dc9305afa7d98be7298a29d36","compact":"5c90eb406c0c6bc0b8ce27dc27649821e1d8ba490a8eed90165002c95eaec62e","nasal":"5c90eb406c0c6bc0b8ce27dc27649821e1d8ba490a8eed90165002c95eaec62e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":17,"english":"And discharged darts at the invincible Rāghava. Thereupon Kākutstha by means of shafts decked with gold, cut off those fourteen darts of theirs. Seeing this, that exceedingly cnergetic one, waxing highly enraged, look out fourteen darts with many golden arrows, whetted on stone, resembling the sun. And even as Satakratu hurls the thunder bolt, Rāghava drawing his bow and taking his aim at the Rākşasas, let go those shafts.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.508,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-15","DUTT-3-20-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bbd2de21f8937c86beb8769ae3c55b8dbdff912a08cd04e8a0b80692615c2f75","compact":"85899e8335a1a30bbefb9c0ba13fc63a063115949e2699313c184b1309e81d91","nasal":"1bebd50146787a945d6c1d7148f12299c0dacb41852ab7b5d6e31d686c307d4f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":18,"english":"Seeing this, that exceedingly cnergetic one, waxing highly enraged, look out fourteen darts with many golden arrows, whetted on stone, resembling the sun. And even as Satakratu hurls the thunder bolt, Rāghava drawing his bow and taking his aim at the Rākşasas, let go those shafts.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cb7822fd1f45f3f1eb506615d010323082c27ce24fb59c392a2b1ec00992c95b","compact":"27743356692e6c0c0c7bec1fb56276b66b66f402c839f0dbafb77df74c471ef0","nasal":"27743356692e6c0c0c7bec1fb56276b66b66f402c839f0dbafb77df74c471ef0"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":19,"english":"Seeing this, that exceedingly cnergetic one, waxing highly enraged, look out fourteen darts with many golden arrows, whetted on stone, resembling the sun. And even as Satakratu hurls the thunder bolt, Rāghava drawing his bow and taking his aim at the Rākşasas, let go those shafts.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c65e85ea543640aff30f2355743b89ffdd865cbfe47f28e3911a9e7111af3de8","compact":"d3d1615ea65a3477ecb24e3efa5f135bc416dca5f874759129dcc8affe9f0447","nasal":"d3d1615ea65a3477ecb24e3efa5f135bc416dca5f874759129dcc8affe9f0447"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":20,"english":"As she said this, Khara wrought up with boundless passion, said, Two human beings accoutred in arins, and wearing bark and dark deer-skins have in company with a female entered this deep Dandaka forest. Do you returni, after slaying them, as well as that wicked one. And this sister of mine will drink their blood.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.429,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-19-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3510eba46ad4c7c3b2044ac0b1bcfde9e655b5ccfda88c595ca0822848c85d84","compact":"38043874d8aa427b75987ac973d5afcf93d1647cab8fc41e327bdea2a701fd0a","nasal":"0b6dd12fae1bb28f9f640da481190f63f0dadc4dab460669fb817cad58c741cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":21,"english":"And those Rākşasas, their breasts pierced with vehemence, and themselves bathed in blood, fell down to the carth, like snakes dropping down from an ant hill.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.553,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"94b86979d0189b18cb5c875e7003011a0ef1f03539217b2346dc82377da63e97","compact":"69ce7477dbe846fa82b741cfbf7a789e011904867104cb023b5b37a1e8b005f6","nasal":"cc51ef553bf6f08e5503bccd91ae1d6c4e79118f0573b2b01e5024096208a0cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":22,"english":"And with their breasts pierced, they, dripping with blood, deformed and deprived of their lives, lay on the ground like trees whose roots have been severed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.594,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"23c49fd513a35ce103a3428452a4df7146befd8dec28d760dd3ade998dfd7b17","compact":"08dd6a7e7080488588791ebe6a8d39eb28c10fbb0df2dc2177d4db4a2427b4bd","nasal":"7cef1a13f7b0bd976e89f3a10e6ae88cafe755d42f9553343467f03f66dbb676"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":23,"english":"Seeing them fallen-on the ground, the Rākşasī, beyond herself in wrath, approaching Khara, with her blood a little dried up, again in distressful guise threw herself on the earth, like a plant exuding gum.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.417,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ec62c685668c70120b2c4c503254b5da32302ac09372a1f06be767c5a346c20","compact":"e12c00d4e3f6c40b5666e279ccb696b84866b15ae19e9fc90007e6913ccf4f0b","nasal":"6b9033c9655ad6688e7cd2d27e03c868ebfe18c13e74a49546f1113693123cac"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":24,"english":"Seeing them fallen-on the ground, the Rākşasī, beyond herself in wrath, approaching Khara, with her blood a little dried up, again in distressful guise threw herself on the earth, like a plant exuding gum.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.652,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65021e587efe4b29edf585ba7cee9d466994c71464d17a417d6ddc7fc6154192","compact":"cc2f3cf3d74c2828a41f8bba3315dc41823f072f7a05652080051ef37cf4ab3a","nasal":"a8d356022e576ac6a144251a0e6a9be4abe074f3309c1c9ed6fca6783016e121"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-19-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":19,"verse":25,"english":"Seeing those Rākşasas slain in battle, Śūrpanakhā again hastened (to his brother); and the sister of Khara, related in detail the slaughter of those Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-20-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3019025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f409049c190ae9856b535a709c769decf863bd04bafa80c3a7e7ea0a37fbaec0","compact":"974e4a4d00edee0d50836cbb33bcc653ccc6443f5c80727994ebfd5b6d6e7cf6","nasal":"974e4a4d00edee0d50836cbb33bcc653ccc6443f5c80727994ebfd5b6d6e7cf6"}}]
